## 15. WHAT NOT TO BUILD YET

- Do **not** add `VECTOR`, `MEMORY`, or `HACKATHON` as runtime `AgentRole`s — they have no spec grounding as named agents (§3) and no implementation justification exists.
- Do **not** rename `CODER`/`RESEARCHER`/`COMPUTER_AUTOMATION`/etc. to `FORGE`/`SCOUT`/`PILOT`/etc. — no contract work has established that correspondence, and doing so on naming grounds alone would be exactly the "renaming to match the roster" the instructions warn against.
- Do **not** build a general-purpose thread-pool/multi-worker executor before the unlocked shared state (§5, `PermissionGateway`, `ApprovalStore`, `ProjectStore`) is addressed — this would be shipping real parallelism on top of components the codebase's own comments already flag as not fully safe for it.
- Do **not** build a generalized resource-locking/claims system yet — current specialist count and workload don't justify it; a coarse project/workspace-identity rule is sufficient for now.
- Do **not** build cost-aware/adaptive-model-selection routing yet — there's no cost/capability-depth data anywhere in the system to route on; this would be premature abstraction over data that doesn't exist.
- Do **not** invent a new numbered phase for any of this — per the instructions, this stays within the existing phase framing until a contract is actually designed and approved.
- Do **not** implement fallback chains beyond the one that already exists until there's a second real, distinct implementation of an existing capability to fall back to (currently there's exactly one implementation per role — a "chain" with one link isn't a chain).

